title: Analytics › Denial reasons
route: /analytics
intro: Why decisions were not approved as requested. A Pareto of the most common reasons with the preventable ones marked, a donut of preventable against not, the preventable denials by payer, and the reasons behind each diagnosis group. Every row, slice and bar opens its cases.
dir: TD
also: A denial is anything not approved as requested, so a cut in days or units counts. Preventable means the team could have fixed the documentation or the timing before sending: thin or missing documentation, late notice, an incomplete certification, a duplicate request.
---
start s1 "Scroll to 'Denial reasons'"
screen sc "'311 denials, 207 of them preventable (67%).'\n'Most common reasons': Continued-stay evidence incomplete 73 (23%), Partial approval without a stated reason 34, Units requested above criteria 34 ...\nA 'Preventable' tag and a striped bar on the preventable ones, a running share on the right, and a dashed line where 80% is reached\n'N other reasons' rolls up the rest"
screen d1 "Donut 'Preventable or not': 207 (67%) and 104 (33%), with a legend\n'Preventable denials by payer' bars"
screen d2 "'Reasons by diagnosis group'\nOne bar for each group, split into four kinds: Documentation or evidence, Timing or notice, Level of care or days, Administrative\nThe number is the group's denials"

click c1 "Click a reason row, for example 'Continued-stay evidence incomplete'"
process p1 "Opens the case list panel for those 73 cases"
decision q1 "Does the reason belong to one payer?"
screen l1 "The panel offers 'Open in Denial Intelligence'\nIt carries the payer and the reason"
goto g1 "Continues in: Denial Intelligence › Open denials list"
screen l2 "A reason two payers give, such as 'Recertification filed too late', lists both payers' cases\nNo Denial Intelligence link"
click c2 "Click a donut slice or its legend row"
process p2 "Opens the preventable or not-preventable denials"
click c3 "Click a payer bar"
process p3 "Opens that payer's preventable denials"
click c4 "Click a diagnosis group bar"
process p4 "Opens that group's denials; hover a segment for its kind and count"
goto g2 "Continues in: Analytics › Case list panel"
click d3 "Click 'View data table' under a chart"
process d4 "A table of the same numbers"

s1 --> sc --> d1 --> d2
sc --> c1 --> p1 --> q1
q1 -->|Yes| l1 --> g1
q1 -->|No| l2
l1 & l2 --> g2
d1 --> c2 --> p2 --> g2
d1 --> c3 --> p3 --> g2
d2 --> c4 --> p4 --> g2
sc --> d3 --> d4
